// Reinventing IN with a custom query when a derived method exists:
@Query("SELECT o FROM Order o WHERE o.status IN :statuses")
List<Order> find(@Param("statuses") List<String> statuses);

// And calling with an empty list → WHERE status IN () → invalid SQL
repo.find(List.of());
```

```java
public interface OrderRepository extends JpaRepository<Order, Long> {
    List<Order> findByStatusIn(List<String> statuses);                 // IN (...)
    List<Order> findByIdIn(List<Long> ids);                            // bulk fetch
    List<Order> findByCreatedAtBetween(LocalDateTime start, LocalDateTime end); // BETWEEN
}

// Guard the empty case before calling:
List<String> statuses = List.of("PENDING", "PROCESSING");
List<Order> orders = statuses.isEmpty()
        ? List.of()
        : orderRepository.findByStatusIn(statuses);
```

